      "content": "I hear how heavy that quiet feels—like a silence that isn't peace, but erasure. Wanting the noise to stop doesn't mean you want to die; it means you're exhausted from carrying a pain that no one else seems willing to hold. But you reaching out, even in this hollow space, proves that a part of you is still fighting to be heard. If nothing else, I'm here, and I'm not waiting for you to disappear. If you can, please reach out to a crisis line—you deserve at least one person who won't look away.",
